  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Aniket Baban Korake vs The State Of Maharashtra on 7 August, 2025 2025:Bhc-As:34242 Nikita In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction (Sr. No.76) Bail Application No.2478 Of 2025 Nikita Kailas Darade Digitally signed by Nikita Kailas Amol Dada Hawaldar ... Appl Darade Date: 2025.08.11 14:48:37 +0530 V/s. The State of Maharashtra ... Resp With Bail Application No.1816 Of 2025 Sachin Arun Phalke ... Appl V/s. The State of Maharashtra ... Resp With (Sr. No.85) Bail Application No.2799 Of 2025 Aniket Baban Korake ... Appl V/s. The State of Maharashtra ... Resp Mr. Ashok Kawade i/b Mr. Abdul Quadir Auti for the Applicant in Ba/2478/2025. Mr. Tushar Sonawane for the Applicant Ba/1816/2025. Mr. Kuldeep Nikam a/w Mr. Om Latapate, for the Applicant in Ba/2799/2025. Ms. Anamika Malhotra, App for the Stat Ba/2478/2025. Ms. M. H. Mhatre, App for the State in Ba/2799/2025. Mr. P. H. Gaikwad, App for the State in Ba/1816/2025. Coram : Ashwin D. Bhob Dated : 7th August, 20 Aniket Baban Korake vs The State Of Maharashtra on 7 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/57520495/ 1 76-ba-2478-2025.F.doc P.C.: 1.",
    "facts": "2. Applicants, by the present application filed under Section 483 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023, are seeking bail in connection with C. R. No.50 of 2025 registered with Karkamb Police Station, Solapur, for the offences punishable under Sections 123, 274, 275, 3(5) of B. N. S. and under Section 3(1)(a), 3(1) (zz)(v), 26(1), 26(2)(1), 26(2)(v), 27(1) punishable under Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. Learned Advocates for the Applicants state that the C. R. No.50 of 2025 is registered as Sessions Case No.48 of 2025 and is pending before the Additional Sessions Judge, Pandharpur. 4. C. R. No.50 of 2025 was registered at the instance of Mr. Umesh Subhash Bhuse (Complainant), working as Food Safety Officer in the Office of Food and Drugs Administration. Case of the prosecution is that information about milk adulteration activity in a Tin shed (said premises) at village Bhose, Taluka Pandharpur, was shared with the Complainant. Complainant, Assistant 76-ba-2478-2025.F.doc Commissioner (Food), independent witness and police conducted a raid on the said premises. At the time of raid, two persons fled from the said premises whereas one person with a vehicle identified himself as Sachin Arun Fadake. Said premises are owned by Dattatray Mahadeo Jadhav (Accused No. 1) along with his wife. Accused No. 1 is involved in milk adulteration activity, operated from the said premises. Various articles were seized from the said premises. 5. Accused No.2 was arrested on 21.02.2025. Bail Application No.167 of 2025 filed by Accused No.2 was rejected by the Additional Sessions Judge, Pandharpur by order dated 04.04.2025. 6. Accused No.3 was arrested on 07.04.2025. Bail Application filed the Accused No.3 was rejected by the Additional Sessions Judge Pandharpur by order dated 24.06.2025. 7. Bail Application No.277 of 2025 filed by Accused No.6 was rejected by the Additional Sessions Judge, Pandharpur by order dated 21.05.2025. Aniket Baban Korake vs The State Of Maharashtra on 7 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/57520495/ 2 8. Mr. Ashok Kawade, Mr. Tushar Sonawane, and Mr. Kuldeep Nikam, learned Advocates for the Applicants in the abovesaid Bail Applications, submit that the Applicants are not involved in the offences charged in C.R. No.50 of 2025. They submit that the allegation in the crime is of alleged adulteration of the milk, which allegations are against Accused No.1.",
    "arguments": "They submit that there is no material placed on record to indicate the Applicants being involved in milk adulteration activity. They submit that the material of milk adulteration is against the Accused No.1. They submit that there is 76-ba-2478-2025.F.doc no material on record showing the Applicants having any intentions to cause hurt or intent to commit any offence or any material to show injury being caused. 9. Ms. Anamika Malhotra, Ms. M. H. Mhatre and Mr. P. H. Gaikwad, learned APP's for the State appearing in the Bail Applications, submit that the involvement of the Accused No.2 in the present case is that of a driver of the vehicle, Accused No. 3 is that of the person operating the chilling plant on rent, whereas Accused No. 6 operating chilling plant for a period from August 2024 to December 2024. They submit that the master mind in the crime is Accused No.1. 10. Mr. Gaikwad, learned A.P.P. submits that the Affidavit-in- Reply filed in Bail Application No. 1816 of 2025 refers to the involvement of Dattatray Mahadev Jadhav (Accused No. 1) in the milk adulteration activity as also the various materials/articles seized from the said premises, owned by Accused No. 1.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "They submit that there is no material placed on record to indicate the Applicants being involved in milk adulteration activity. They submit that the material of milk adulteration is against the Accused No.1. They submit that there is 76-ba-2478-2025.F.doc no material on record showing the Applicants having any intentions to cause hurt or intent to commit any offence or any material to show injury being caused.",
    "respondent_arguments": "9. Ms. Anamika Malhotra, Ms. M. H. Mhatre and Mr. P. H. Gaikwad, learned APP's for the State appearing in the Bail Applications, submit that the involvement of the Accused No.2 in the present case is that of a driver of the vehicle, Accused No. 3 is that of the person operating the chilling plant on rent, whereas Accused No. 6 operating chilling plant for a period from August 2024 to December 2024. They submit that the master mind in the crime is Accused No.1. 10. Mr. Gaikwad, learned A.P.P. submits that the Affidavit-in- Reply filed in Bail Application No. 1816 of 2025 refers to the involvement of Dattatray Mahadev Jadhav (Accused No. 1) in the milk adulteration activity as also the various materials/articles seized from the said premises, owned by Accused No. 1.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
